{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - Account - Administrator Role Assigned to an Okta User",
	"Description": "An administrator role was granted to an Okta user. This is the single most direct privilege escalation in Okta: the granted account can then change policies, create API tokens, and add identity providers.\n\nEvent type: user.account.privilege.grant\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/persistence_administrator_role_assigned_to_okta_user/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta/persistence_administrator_role_assigned_to_okta_user.toml\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "a7179065-d545-5188-87ba-9b5a74476b6d",
	"SearchReference": "c475683a-507a-5981-adb9-1b95d469f0e3"
